.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-BAR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-bar
.Nd the Patina desktop's bar
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar config.toml
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the bar along the bottom (or top) of the screen.
Its buttons and icons open the launcher and the tray's menus, its tabs are
the list of open windows, and its config file holds the settings the whole
shell shares: the skin and the wallpaper.
.Pp
It holds modules on the left, in the centre and on the right:
.Bl -tag -width launcher
.It Ic launcher
The Sector F flask, which opens the launcher.
.It Ic windows
A tab per open window, with its app's icon and its name and title, as
.Ic window_tabs
says.
The text is the app's name from its
.Pa .desktop
entry, then the window's title, as
.Dq Files - Home ;
just the name when the title only names the app, and without a last part
of the title that names it again, so Firefox's
.Dq Patina \(em Mozilla Firefox
is
.Dq Firefox - Patina .
A click focuses it, a middle click closes it; the compositor's Alt+Tab
and Super+1 to 9 follow the same order, and hovering one of the first nine
says its key.
The apps in
.Ic pinned
come first, each as its windows' tabs, or, with none open, a faded icon
that starts it.
Dragging a tab moves it: a pinned app's among the pins; another window's,
dropped among the pins, pins its app there, and dropped among the other
windows, moves it along them, which
.Xr patina-compositor 1
keeps, so its keys follow.
A right click opens its menu, in
.Xr patina-menu 1
so it isn't cut off at the bar's edge: New Window opens another window of
its app,
by the
.Pa .desktop
entry's
.Dq new-window
action if it has one, else by its
.Ic Exec ;
Pin to Bar or Unpin from Bar; and Close Window.
A pinned app with no window offers Open and Unpin from Bar.
Hovering a tab, or an icon in the tray, shows its tooltip a moment later,
also in
.Xr patina-menu 1 ,
past the bar's edge.
The icon is the one the app's
.Pa .desktop
entry names, found by the window's app id.
.It Ic tray
Apps' status icons, such as Steam's: the bar is the system tray they
register with
.Pq Sy org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher
on the session bus, the StatusNotifierItem protocol libappindicator speaks.
A click activates the app (or opens the menu of one that's only a menu), a
middle click is its secondary action, and a right click opens its menu in
.Xr patina-menu 1 ,
submenus folded in as
.Dq Parent \(Fo Item ;
hovering shows its name.
After them, with more than one keyboard layout, the one in use, as
.Dq US ;
a click lists them to switch to another, which Ctrl+Space also does.
Then Wi-Fi, which opens
.Xr patina-wifi 1 ;
the speaker, which opens
.Xr patina-volume 1 ;
and the battery, red at 10% or less while discharging, which opens
.Xr patina-settings 1
at its Power page.
.It Ic clock
The time.
.It Ic power
The power button, after the clock, which opens
.Xr patina-power 1 :
Lock, Log Out, Restart and Shut Down.
.It Ic tags , layout , title , appid
dwl's status, when the bar is dwl's status command.
.El
.Pp
It's started by
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
and started again whenever it exits.
It runs on any compositor with wlr-layer-shell, and as dwl's status
command
.Pq Ql dwl -s patina-bar ,
reading dwl's status from its standard input.
.Pp
The menus and the launcher are opened with the bar's skin and edge in
.Ev PATINA_SKIN
and
.Ev PATINA_BAR_EDGE .
Under
.Xr patina-compositor 1
they're started by the compositor, so they're listed with their output in
Settings' Processes page; anywhere else the bar starts them itself.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , -config Ar file
Read
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml .
.It Fl -section Cm launcher | windows | tray | reserve- Ns Ar edge
Draw one part of a split bar (see
.Ic layout ) .
The bar starts these itself, with its pipe on their standard input, and
they end when it closes; there's no need to run them by hand.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml ,
TOML; every key is optional.
The bar reads it again within a second of a change, and the other pieces
read it when they open.
It also follows
.Ic [gaps]
in
.Xr patina-compositor 1 Ns 's
config: with gaps on, it floats the gap away from the screen's edges, with
rounded corners.
.Xr patina-menu 1
and
.Xr patina-settings 1
write
.Ic skin ,
.Ic wallpaper ,
.Ic window_tabs
and
.Ic position ,
and the bar writes
.Ic pinned ,
keeping the rest of the file.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic position
.Dq bottom
(the default) or
.Dq top .
.It Ic height
In logical pixels; 41 by default.
.It Ic window_tabs
What each window's tab shows:
.Dq both ,
its app's icon and its title (the default);
.Dq icons ,
narrow tabs with only the icon and the title on hover; or
.Dq titles .
.It Ic pinned
The apps pinned to the window tabs, by app id, in order, as
.Ql pinned = ["firefox", "org.gnome.Nautilus"] ;
none by default.
.Xr patina-compositor 1
reads it too, so Super+1 to 9 reach the same tabs.
.It Ic layout
.Dq bar ,
one bar along an edge (the default); or
.Dq split
(experimental): its parts each on their own, the launcher, the window list
and the rest
.Pq the tray, the clock, the power button ,
where
.Ic launcher_at ,
.Ic windows_at
and
.Ic tray_at
say.
The bar draws the window list and runs the other parts as
.Ql patina-bar --section ;
each edge with a part on it is kept clear of windows by a pixel-thin strip
that takes no clicks.
The bar starts itself again, laid out anew, within a second of a change to
these keys.
.It Ic launcher_at , windows_at , tray_at
Where each part of a split bar goes: an edge, then where along it.
Along the top or bottom a part is a row:
.Dq top-left ,
.Dq top-center ,
.Dq top-right ,
.Dq bottom-left ,
.Dq bottom-center
or
.Dq bottom-right .
Up a side it's a column, the window list one of icons:
.Dq left-top ,
.Dq left-center ,
.Dq left-bottom ,
.Dq right-top ,
.Dq right-center
or
.Dq right-bottom .
A column at a side's end sits past a row in that corner, and a part sharing
the launcher's spot lines up after it; other parts in one spot overlap.
By default the launcher is at the bottom left, the window list in the
bottom centre and the tray at the bottom right.
Settings' Bar page places them by dragging them on a map of the screen.
.It Ic skin
A Patina skin by name: a built-in, or one in
.Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/skins .
.It Ic left , center , right
The modules on each side, as lists:
.Dl left = [\(dqlauncher\(dq, \(dqwindows\(dq]
.It Ic clock
A
.Xr strftime 3
format;
.Dq %a %-d %b  %H:%M
by default.
.It Ic launcher , volume , wifi , battery , power
What the flask, the speaker, the Wi-Fi icon, the battery and the power button run,
through
.Xr sh 1 .
.It Ic wallpaper
An image file, drawn by
.Xr patina-wallpaper 1 ;
empty for the default.
.It Ic tags , hide_vacant_tags
A label per dwl tag, and whether to hide tags with no windows.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN , PATINA_BAR_EDGE
Set for what the bar opens: its skin, and
.Dq top
or
.Dq bottom .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml
The settings above.
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/skins/
Skins of your own.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Restart the bar after installing a new one; the compositor starts it
again:
.Pp
.Dl $ pkill -x patina-bar
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-power 1 ,
.Xr patina-settings 1 ,
.Xr patina-volume 1 ,
.Xr patina-wallpaper 1 ,
.Xr patina-wifi 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
